Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS)
The Analogy: Renting a standard car. The rental agency provides the vehicle, engine, tires, and maintenance. However, you must drive it, choose the route, buy the gas, and ensure you don't crash.

What You Get: Empty virtual hardware — raw virtual machines, hard drives, and network routers.

Who Manages What:

Provider handles: Physical servers, cooling, electricity, hypervisors, and data center security.

You handle: Installing/updating the Operating System (Linux/Windows), applying security patches, configuring firewalls, and installing software.

Real-World Examples:

Amazon EC2 (AWS): Spinning up a blank Ubuntu virtual server.

Google Compute Engine (GCE): Provisioning raw computing instances.

Microsoft Azure Virtual Machines.
